{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>On the sabbath.</b> It reverts to the day of the sabbath, even though every keeper of the sabbath is [already] found [as one who would] profane it. And the meaning is: every sabbath and sabbath, like יום ביומו (day by day)." "<b>Beside the continual burnt-offering.</b> The meaning is: after the continual offering, that he places upon it the burnt-offering of the sabbath."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The phrase 'found profaning it' is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. The argument appears compressed and opaque as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:46.084745549Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}